Title: LAST LIGHT
Credit: a seriesmith demo scene
Draft date: 2026-10-17

FADE IN:

EXT. CITY SKYLINE - NIGHT

Rain sheets across a canyon of neon towers. Far below, traffic crawls like lava. High on one rooftop, a single blue light is moving fast.

EXT. ROOFTOP - WATER TOWERS - NIGHT

MARA KESS (20s), a courier in a cropped yellow rain jacket, hood down, braids whipping, sprints between rusted water towers. Strapped across her back: THE CASE, a battered steel briefcase with a seam of blue light pulsing along its edge.

Her boots smash through a puddle. Neon bleeds across the water.

Behind her, a door BANGS open. VOSS (40s), tall, grey longcoat, mirrored visor over his eyes, steps into the rain. He doesn't run. He doesn't need to.

                    VOSS
          That case isn't yours, Kess.

Mara doesn't look back.

                    MARA
          Neither's the city. I'm borrowing both.

EXT. ROOFTOP - EDGE - NIGHT

The roof ends. A gap, ten feet wide, a sixty-storey drop. Across it, the next roof, a forest of satellite dishes.

Mara doesn't slow down. She plants a boot on the ledge and LAUNCHES.

Mid-air. Rain hangs around her. The case's light streaks a blue arc across the dark.

She hits the far roof, rolls through the landing, comes up running.

EXT. ROOFTOP - SATELLITE DISHES - NIGHT

Voss reaches the ledge behind her. Stops. Touches his visor. It flickers red.

Out of the rain rises a DRONE, black, four rotors, a red eye. It tilts toward Mara and screams after her.

Mara weaves between the dishes. The drone's red beam sweeps the roof, cutting through the rain.

A dish EXPLODES in sparks a step behind her.

EXT. ROOFTOP - CABLE - NIGHT

At the far corner, a power cable sags across the street to a lower building.

Mara whips off her belt, loops it over the cable, grips both ends, and jumps.

She slides down the cable, sparks spitting from the belt, the city rushing up beneath her.

The drone dives after her.

EXT. ROOFTOP - EDGE - NIGHT

Voss watches, rain running off his visor.

                    VOSS
                    (into his collar)
          She's on the line. Cut it.

EXT. LOWER ROOF - NIGHT

Mara lets go a breath before the cable SNAPS. She drops, hits a gravel roof, slides to a stop at its edge.

Behind her, the drone tangles in the falling cable and spins down into the street in a shower of sparks.

Silence but for the rain.

Mara unslings the case. She thumbs the latch. It opens.

Inside, nested in foam: a single seedling in a glass bulb, its leaves glowing the same soft blue.

Mara smiles.

                    MARA
          Still alive. Good. Let's get you home.

She closes the case, shoulders it, and steps off the edge into the dark.

SMASH CUT TO BLACK.
